course: dictionary
lesson: 11332
title: Place names with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Names of places always start with a capital letter, because they are special names. York is a name, so it is written with a big Y. In «New York», York is the second part of the name, so both words start with a capital letter.
explain: York can mean more than one place. Most often it is New York, a big city and a state in the USA. It can also mean York, an old city in the north of England, famous for its walls and its cathedral. A third York is in Canada, where Toronto was once called York.
explain: Read the words around York to work out which place is meant. If the sentence mentions England, the Romans or the Vikings, it is the English city. If it mentions skyscrapers, the Statue of Liberty or America, it is New York. The clues tell you which one it is.
fact: York is a proper noun, a special name, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: York in England is an old city in the north, famous for its walls, its cathedral (York Minster) and the Vikings.
fact: New York is a big city and a state in the USA, with the Statue of Liberty and skyscrapers.
fact: The English city of York was a Roman and Viking town.
fact: In «New York», York is part of the name, so both words start with capital letters.
exercise: «A boy in New York practised the drums for hours every day.» Which place is York in this sentence? | York, an old city in the north of England | A cathedral called York Minster | *New York, a big city in the USA | York in Canada
exercise: «The Erie Canal ... helping New York become the leading port of the United States.» Why is York written with a capital letter? | It is the first word of the sentence | *It is part of a place name | It is the name of a person | It is a colour
exercise: Which fact is about York in England? | *Its walls and cathedral are famous | It has skyscrapers and the Statue of Liberty | It is where Toronto got its first name | It is a state in the USA
test: «Millions of immigrants came to America ... and Ellis Island in New York.» Which words are clues that York means New York here? | Toronto was once called York | Roman and Viking | *The Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island | Walls and a cathedral
test: Noon in London, but «still early morning in New York». Is New York in England? | Yes, it is in Canada | Yes, it is a Viking town | Yes, it is in the north, near the walls | *No, it is in the USA
exam: «Jean-Michel Basquiat started as a graffiti writer in New York.» Which York is meant here? | A Roman fort in Scotland | *New York, the big city and state in the USA | York in Canada | York, the old English city with the Minster
